# Line budgets, enforced by verifyE2eHarness (e2e/tools/verify/verify-line-budgets.sh). Each number lives here only.
# Raising one needs its own commit that says why: the budget is what keeps the harness and the skill small enough
# to be read whole.
#
# e2e/scripts/{shared,android,ios}: every file, in lines. The plan said 3500; the harness grew past it with the
# adapters, the environment check and the verdict. 4700 after the audit corrections (the plan said 3500, the first value 4500); the owner's ceiling is 5000.
# Round 3 (H): 5040, 330 lines over the previous 4710 for the driver-contract verb of both adapters and its readers, the degraded
# simulator (classification, health, recovery rule), the tolerance counts and the series count. Past the owner's 5000: the
# orchestrating session fixes the final number.
# The remate (prepare and launch times) brought the use to 5040; 5060 left room.
# Delta audit corrections: area C removed about 45 lines of duplicated and dead code and added the thresholds and counts of the
# degraded simulator, the ledger's seams, the driver log of a killed run, refusals apart from tolerances, the stricter Android
# probe reader and the finish of a cut series; area D (ΔD-10) moved under the fingerprint the 175 lines of the shared shell
# library that the build and the harness execute (e2e/scripts/shared/ci-common.sh), which were counted nowhere before.
# The orchestrating session fixes the final number at the close.
# Option C (the CI never writes evidence): `publish` cites trusted evidence from an ancestor (e2e.py, publish.py, verdict.py),
# +14 lines over 5400. The orchestrating session fixes the final number.
E2E_SCRIPTS_MAX_LINES=5420
# The skill: its entry point and its runbook. The entry point is firm. The runbook went from 300 to 320 with the delta audit:
# the driver-contract gate, the degraded-simulator rule, refusals and tolerances, the seam rule and what the fingerprint covers.
SKILL_MD_MAX_LINES=140
CERTIFICATION_RUNBOOK_MAX_LINES=320
